the falcon and the winter soldier is  full of everything that makes the mcu  special  action super powers witty jokes and of  course a ton of easter eggs for the  attentive fan  here are a few you might have missed in  episode 2 the star-spangled man  just before bucky barnes and sam attempt  to jump the flag smashers the two have  one of many hilarious exchanges in an  abandoned warehouse  bucky's stealthy behavior prompts sam to  call him the white panther as a joke  referencing the time bucky spent in  wakanda after the events of captain  america civil war  bucky quickly corrects him it's actually  why wolf  this confuses sam for a moment but the  scene moves on without further  discussion we first see bucky referred  to as the white wolf in the second  post-credits scene from black panther  some village children refer to bucky by  this name while he's residing in wakanda  under the watch of shuri  t'challa later calls bucky this name  during avengers infinity war before  giving him a new vibranium arm for the  impending battle against thanos army  the falcon of the winter soldier marks  the first time we've heard bucky revert  to himself as the white wolf  in the comics the winter soldier and the  white wolf aren't the same character  instead the white wolf is hunter  t'challa's adopted white brother  king t'chaka takes hunter in as an  infant after he crash lands in wakanda  with his parents who don't make it out  of the wreckage alive  he eventually becomes the leader of the  wakandan secret police and takes on the  white wolf moniker  while john walker the new captain  america is practicing for his first big  interview he's greeted by a friend who  gives him a pep talk  later this man officially introduces  himself as lamar hoskins to sam and  bucky after the tractor-trailer highway  battle and even reveals his hero name  battle star first appearing in 1986 is  captain america number 323  hoskins was a wrestler until he was  granted superhuman abilities by the  power broker his bond with john walker  is strong  the two are picked by the government to  be the new cap and bucky this explains  why our bucky gets angry at the mention  of battlestar and hops out of the car  when he and sam talk to the pair after  the highway battle  in the comics hoskins is part of a group  called the bold urban commandos  aka the buckies the buckies and walker  are known at this time as super patriot  battle steve rogers and lose some time  after this the government taps walker to  become the new captain america and  hoskins as the new bucky the latter  eventually dubs himself battlestar  in 1989's captain america number 350  steve regains the mantle of captain  america prompting battlestar to retire  to his hometown of chicago  as an angry sam and bucky walk away from  their highway battle defeats in the  star-spangled man  walker and hoskins ride up on them bucky  tells walker that holding the shield  doesn't mean he's captain america and  asks if walker has ever jumped on top of  a grenade  yeah actually i have four times the  thing i do with my helmet it's a  reinforced  helmet it's a long story it's not  exactly the same thing that our friend  steve rogers does in captain america the  first avenger  while training in boot camp colonel  chester phillips tosses a dead grenade  at a group of his recruits to see how  they respond  without hesitation rogers still weak and  skinny at this point dives on top of the  grenade to absorb the explosion and  protect those around him  it's one of the character's most  memorable and moving heroic deeds  and bucky's subtle invocation of it  speaks volumes  we meet isaiah bradley and the  star-spangled man after bucky and sam  fail in their fight against the flag  smashers  in a brief conversation we learned that  bucky and isaiah have battled one  another in the past and that the latter  was actually able to rip off half of  bucky's arm  first appearing in 2003's truth red  white and black number one  isaiah is sometimes known as the black  captain america  he and 299 other black soldiers are  experimented on as part of governmental  efforts to replicate the super soldier  serum  though isaiah shows enormous bravery  during world war ii is court-martialed  and imprisoned for 17 brutal years  in the falcon and the winter soldier  isaiah reveals he was in jail for 30  years during which constant tests were  performed upon him  bucky let sam know that isaiah is a hero  and is feared by hydra as steve rogers  was  one of the ones that hydra fear the most  like steve  founded by curtis jackson power broker  is both an organization and a man first  appearing in 1978's machine man number  seven  jackson aims to profit from making super  soldiers despite the extreme riskiness  of the process in the comics the power  broker transforms both john walker and  lamar hoskins into super soldiers  their superhuman strength is hinted at  during the highway battle seen in the  star-spangled man  when bucky mentions that the flag  smashers are super soldiers hoskins acts  surprised by the term  as though he doesn't know such people  exist beyond steve rogers and bucky  this could be an effort to throw bucky  off descent if hoskins is in fact  already a super soldier himself  it's suspected that the power broker is  responsible for the flag smasher's  superhuman abilities  but one of their members mentions the  power brokers man are the ones coming  after them during the private plane  escape scene  we don't yet know why they're being  chased by the power broker but it could  be an effort to de-augment them  jackson's a dr carl malus experiments  with that process on battlestar  in the comics luckily walker saves his  pal in the nick of time  as always if you want to impress your  friends with your marvel easter egg  knowledge you need to pay close  attention to any numbers that appear on  screen  at the end of the star spangled man  there's a quick shot of zemo in prison  with the footage noting that his cell  number is 2187  no need to hunt your back issues though  since this isn't actually a reference to  zemo's comic book origins  instead it's a reference to a different  story from a long time ago in a galaxy  far  far away in star wars a new hope  princess leia's cell number is 2187  a number that reappears in the force  awakens where it's used as finn's  stormtrooper designation  both appearances of the number are  actually a reference to 2187 a national  film board of canada's short that  inspired a young george lucas  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite comic book heroes and  villains are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

